    {
      "input": "*He asks Bram Kessel who they think he is and where he comes from.*",
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Bram Kessel looks Nicco up and down—a tall, overweight man with scattered white hairs and the first soft recession at his temples. The grinder's hands rest on his hips, flour-dusted apron swaying slightly. \"You're asking me?\" He chuckles, a low rumble. \"You're the one standing on my regular patch, friend. I haven't the faintest where you hail from. West District, by your look—could be anywhere in it. I've not seen your face before, so you're not one of my standing orders.\" He tilts his head, the charcoal stub behind his ear catching the light. \"Why? You want me to guess, or you fixing to tell me?\"",
